<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polycrates</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 522 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Polycrates of Samos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Polycrates was tyrant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a> from about 538 to 522 BCE. With a fleet of a hundred penteconters and a thousand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a> he made Samos the leading naval power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>, raiding widely and allying first with Amasis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and then with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-ii">Cambyses II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunnel-of-eupalinos">Tunnel of Eupalinos</a>, the harbour mole and the great temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a>, and hosted poets such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anacreon">Anacreon</a>, before the Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oroetes">Oroetes</a> had him killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polycrates.jpg" alt="Polycrates" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author Published in 1890 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polykrates_with_Pharao_Amasis_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
